# Your own additions to the allow list. ./agybox copies this file to allow/local.txt, which git ignores.
# Changes apply at once, to running sessions too. ./agybox hosts lists what the proxy refused.
#
# Each host you add is somewhere the agent can send what it can read. An agent that can reach github.com with a
# token can push your workspace to any repository the token allows, or post it as a gist.

# git over HTTPS (git honors the proxy; ssh does not go through it)
# github.com
# codeload.github.com
# objects.githubusercontent.com

# Python packages
# pypi.org
# files.pythonhosted.org

# npm
# registry.npmjs.org

# Ubuntu packages, if you run apt in a docker or apptainer image you build yourself
# archive.ubuntu.com:80
# security.ubuntu.com:80
